---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OptImage from '../../components/OptImage.astro';

const products = await getCollection('products');
const analyzers = products
  .filter((p) => p.data.category === 'analyzer')
  .sort((a, b) => (a.data.order ?? 0) - (b.data.order ?? 0));

const siteUrl = 'https://migibio.net';
const schema = {
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      '@id': `${siteUrl}/equipment/#list`,
      name: 'Veterinary Immunofluorescence Quantitative Analyzers',
      numberOfItems: analyzers.length,
      itemListElement: analyzers.map((p, i) => ({
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: i + 1,
        name: p.data.title,
        url: `${siteUrl}/equipment/${p.data.slug}/`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Equipment — Veterinary Immunofluorescence Analyzers"
  description="Migibio FIA680 (single-channel) and FIA880 (six-channel) veterinary immunofluorescence quantitative analyzers for rapid, quantitative POCT diagnostics."
  schema={schema}
  canonical="/equipment/"
  pageType="CollectionPage"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Equipment' }]}
>
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-800 to-brand-600 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Equipment</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-brand-100">Quantitative fluorescence immunoassay analyzers for veterinary point-of-care diagnostics.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none mb-10 prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-p:text-gray-700 prose-a:text-brand-600 prose-th:text-gray-900 prose-td:text-gray-700 prose-table:border-collapse prose-th:border prose-th:border-gray-300 prose-th:bg-gray-50 prose-th:px-4 prose-th:py-2 prose-td:border prose-td:border-gray-300 prose-td:px-4 prose-td:py-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Choosing an Analyzer</h2>
      <p>Both analyzers use Migibio's fluorescence immunochromatography (FICT) platform and share the same core performance — pg/ml-level sensitivity and CV% under 10% precision — with the full range of canine and feline reagent panels, so the decision comes down to workflow volume and footprint:</p>
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-gray-200">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Feature</th><th>FIA680</th><th>FIA880</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Channels</td><td>Single-channel</td><td>Six independent channels</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Result time</td><td>3–11 minutes</td><td>3–15 minutes</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Throughput</td><td>Up to 200 tests/hour</td><td>Up to 300 tests/hour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Temperature control</td><td>—</td><td>Constant-temperature</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Printer</td><td>Built-in thermal printer</td><td>Built-in thermal printer + A4 export</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Mobile vets, small practices, on-site farm diagnostics</td><td>Reference labs, multi-clinician hospitals, high-volume networks</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>For a detailed side-by-side walkthrough, see <a href="/blog/fia680-vs-fia880-analyzer">FIA680 vs FIA880: Which Analyzer Fits Your Practice</a>. Both units include built-in thermal printing, multi-language interfaces (Chinese, English, Russian, Italian), and cloud standard-curve support via Wi-Fi.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">What the analyzer actually measures</h2>
      <p>The analyzer reads the fluorescence signal from a completed test device. It is not a visual line reader and it does not infer a result from colour intensity alone: the instrument excites the fluorophores, converts the emitted signal through the stored standard curve and reports a concentration in the unit defined by the reagent IFU.</p>
      <p>That distinction matters when comparing systems. A reader with a stable optical path, temperature control and a locked standard curve can support serial monitoring; a device that reports only positive or negative cannot show a trend. Ask for the assay menu, the sample types, the measuring range and the lot-to-lot precision data for the tests you intend to run.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">What to confirm in a demo</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Assay menu:</strong> the canine and feline tests you actually use, not only the flagship menu.</li>
        <li><strong>Workflow:</strong> sample preparation, device loading, result time and what happens when a test is interrupted.</li>
        <li><strong>Data:</strong> how results are stored, exported and connected to the cloud standard curve.</li>
        <li><strong>Training:</strong> who trains the operators, and what documentation remains after the demo.</li>
        <li><strong>Service:</strong> response route, spare parts and software update process, in writing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The right analyzer is the one that fits the clinic's daily queue and the tests it can support, not simply the one with the highest headline throughput.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {analyzers.map((p) => (
        <a href={`/equipment/${p.data.slug}`} class="group overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white shadow-sm transition-shadow hover:shadow-md">
          <div class="aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden bg-gray-100">
            {p.data.image ? (
              <OptImage src={p.data.image} alt={p.data.title} class="h-full w-full object-contain p-4 transition-transform group-hover:scale-105" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 360px" />
            ) : (
              <div class="flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center bg-brand-50"><span class="text-5xl text-brand-300">🔬</span></div>
            )}
          </div>
          <div class="p-5">
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 group-hover:text-brand-700">{p.data.title}</h2>
            {p.data.description && <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 line-clamp-2">{p.data.description}</p>}
            <span class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center text-sm font-medium text-brand-600">View details →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
